@@ -10997,6 +10997,29 @@ Tests: `Radicle/tests/test_avm2_frame_listeners.cpp` has `Avm2FrameListeners.Two
 
 With `FO4_DATA_DIR`, the test passes, and `ran` is 7. Its `R8_HASH` lines (program, frame hash, host-log hash, BGS calls) are AtomicCommand 15, GJ_Defrag 30, Grognak 2, PipFall 10, RedMenace 8, TurretHack 5 and ZetaInvaders 6. They are the same with and without the render dispatch. The test fails on any handler failure, and none occurred. `Radicle/testdata/swf/program_replay_pins.txt` has no rows, so the file does not pin these counts. TurretHack's 5 matches the round-5 note. The other six were compared only with this round's no-render baseline. `ComparesTheCapturedBgsSequenceForEachProgram` skips here, because it needs `FO4_SWF_CAPTURE_DIR` and this machine has no captures.
 
+## Radicle/src/nif/skin_checks.cpp:bind_fault
+
+"Bind transforms present" means the BSSkin::Instance data ref names a BSSkin::BoneData block. `read_bones` returns identity bones without it, so the reader alone cannot show this.
+
+## Radicle/src/nif/skin_checks.cpp:weight_fault
+
+A vertex's weights must sum to 1 within 0.001: four half-float weights of at most 1.0 round by at most 4 x 2^-12. Vertices with zero total weight are not judged, because vanilla has them (`Meshes\Actors\Robot\Parts\HeadSentryType1.nif`).
+
+## Radicle/src/nif/lint_checks.cpp:lint_checks
+
+Measured clean on 226,454 vanilla NIFs and 23,587 skinned shapes. Deliberately absent, because they fire on vanilla: unused strings, triangles repeating a vertex, and sphere enclosure. Vanilla spheres are approximate: `Meshes\Interface\Objects\PADashPipboyScreenSUW.nif` misses by 184%. So only an unset sphere is reported, and skinned shapes, which store zero spheres, are skipped.
+
+## Radicle/src/nif/lint_checks.cpp:relative_texture_path
+
+An absolute path, with a drive letter or leading separator, is cut at its first Textures folder segment that has a file after it. Otherwise the result is empty and no fix is offered.
+
+## Radicle/src/nif/lint_fixes.cpp:lint_fixes
+
+Relocation, then sphere refit (centre = bounds centre, radius = max distance). It runs after the trim loop in `Radicle/src/nif/fix_nif.cpp:fix_nif`, otherwise a path trimmed to absolute stays unfixed and a second fix changes bytes.
+
+## Radicle/src/nif/verify.cpp:verify_nif
+
+Skin then lint checks follow the original ten; the order is the contract, 15 checks in all.
